{
 "help": "usage: wgsextract vcf table [-h] [--vcf-input VCF_INPUT] [--gene GENE] [--genes GENES]\n                            [--gene-file FILE] [--preset NAME] [--bed FILE] [--pad-kb PAD_KB]\n                            [-r REGION] [--sample SAMPLE] [--all-alleles] [--pharmcat-json FILE]\n                            [--no-sqlite] [--format {tsv,parquet}]\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --vcf-input VCF_INPUT\n                        Input VCF file path.\n  --gene GENE           Keep a gene by symbol (repeatable).\n  --genes GENES         Comma-separated gene symbols (repeatable).\n  --gene-file FILE      File of gene symbols (whitespace or comma-separated; # starts a comment).\n  --preset NAME         Gene panel preset (repeatable): pharmacogenes, hla, autoimmune, acmg-sf,\n                        cardiac\n  --bed FILE            BED or BED.gz panel, unioned with the selected gene spans.\n  --pad-kb PAD_KB       Padding on each side of a gene span, in kb (default: 0).\n  -r, --region REGION   Chromosomal region(s); when a panel is given, restrict its union to these\n                        regions.\n  --sample SAMPLE       Sample whose genotypes to use (default: the first).\n  --all-alleles         Also export ALT alleles the sample doesn't carry (0/0 calls, no-calls, the\n                        other ALT of a 0/1 multi-allelic site).\n  --pharmcat-json FILE  PharmCAT's <stem>.phenotype.json (from 'vcf pharmcat'), to add its\n                        diplotype and phenotype to rows in those genes.\n  --no-sqlite           Write only the table file.\n  --format {tsv,parquet}\n                        Table file format: tsv, or parquet (needs pyarrow) (default: tsv)\n\nglobal options:\n  -i/--input, -o/--outdir, --genome, --ref, -t/--threads, -m/--memory, --json, --quiet, --debug,\n  --config and the other global options are accepted before or after the command; 'wgsextract\n  --help' lists them all.\n\nexamples:\n  wgsextract vcf table --vcf-input sample.vcf.gz --bed targets.bed\n  wgsextract vcf table --vcf-input sample.vcf.gz --preset acmg-sf --region chr17\n  wgsextract vcf table --vcf-input clinvar_annotated.vcf.gz --format parquet\n\noutputs (in the output directory unless noted):\n  <input stem>_variants.tsv (or .parquet with --format parquet) and <input\n  stem>_variants.sqlite: one row per variant allele, with its annotations.\n\nneeds:\n  bcftools; depending on options and inputs, also: bgzip, tabix; minutes on a\n  30x genome.\n",
